course: dictionary
lesson: 4363
title: Sound words: gurgle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they describe. Gurgle is one of them. Say it out loud and it sounds like bubbling water. These are sound words, and they help the reader hear the scene.
explain: «When you pull the plug in the bath, the water gurgles away down the drain.» Here gurgles is a verb: it tells you what the water does, which is to make a bubbling sound as it flows.
explain: Gurgle can also be a noun, a thing: «the gurgle of the stream» means the bubbling sound the stream makes. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «the water bubbles away down the drain» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Gurgle means a bubbling sound made by water or liquid as it flows.
fact: A baby also gurgles when it makes happy bubbling sounds in its throat.
fact: As a noun, a gurgle is one such bubbling sound, as in «the gurgle of the stream».
fact: Sound words like gurgle are called onomatopoeia.
fact: Writers use sound words to help the reader hear the scene, such as «a gurgling stream».
exercise: «When you pull the plug in the bath, the water gurgles away down the drain.» What is gurgling here? | The drain pipe being pulled | A bath toy | *The water, making a bubbling sound
exercise: Gurgle is a sound word. What is a sound word? | A word that is spelled backwards | *A word that sounds like the thing it describes | A word with lots of letters
exercise: «the gurgle of the stream» What is a gurgle in this phrase? | *A bubbling sound | A stone in the stream | A fish swimming
test: «People can hear it gurgling in its burrow.» Which word in this sentence is the sound word? | people | *gurgling | burrow | hear
test: «The bottle springs back and outside air is pushed in with a gurgle.» What is a gurgle here? | A squeezing hand | A bottle cap | *A bubbling sound as air rushes in | A sweet tomato sauce
exam: Which use of gurgle is a noun? | The tummy gurgles loudly | *the gurgle of the stream | Gurgling in its burrow | The bath gurgles
